Z||000008||Racer 1||12-23-1999||08:36 AM||||Merry Christmas to everyone "except jews and Joe-Hoe-Fas-Witness people" no offense to them. I had them Joe-Hoe-Fas-Witness people trying to pass out a free flyer about Jesus last week. They always say the dumbest stuff like "Do you know about jesus" or "Have you heard about god lately" one day im gonna dress up like a grim reeper and open the door with a ketchup soaked knife. Everyone drive safe watch for them drunks and weird people around new years.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-23-1999||08:48 AM||||I don't normally discuss religion or politics (well, politics might be OK...Vote for the Monkey and the dog in 2004!!!), but what's wrong with someone asking about Jesus?  I like him.  If you mean that they think that nobody knows about Him, then I agree that that's kind of a dumb thought.  Everyone should know about Him, right?  (If you're wondering if I'm a Christian, then absolutely, positively YES I am.)  I just don't go around like them and try to push my beliefs on everyone else.  They do tend to get a little pushy.  I think that just pushes people away from God.  Next time one of them knocks on your door (and you know FOR SURE that it's them), try answering the door naked and inviting them in.  They won't return.  I hope I haven't offended anyone.  If I have, feel free to email me privately and I will apologize.||||reg||1
