Z||000019||Patrick||12-23-1999||04:14 PM||||<BR>A millennium is one thousand years.<P>As of January 1st 2000, one thousand nine hundred and ninety-nine years and ONE DAY will have passed since the birth of Christ (which is what our calendar system is based on).<P>Remember, there was no such thing as year Zero. The first year was One. (Ogre remembers. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) <P>You can't properly celebrate the beginning of a new millennium until you've passed through the previous one.<P>My two cents worth...||||reg||1
Z||000020||fiero56||12-23-1999||04:54 PM||||Patrik,<BR>you sound a lot like my sister. Being home for the last several weeks from school, every time the tv,radio,friends,neigbors,etc mention the new millenium she just has to set everyone straight. Reminds me of people talking about how they set someone straight when asked "aren't those the cars that caught fire?". She has all these articles out of magazines talking about how/why the new millenium doesn't start for another year. <BR>Most of us know that, but whos gonna' sit around as the calendar goes from 1999 to 2000. Thats alot more exciting than seeing 2000 to 2001. At least for me.<BR>This month Popular Mechanics put out an entire page about the whole millenium bit. This isn't a flame. I just wrote it so the "next year" people know, we know. We just can't wait another year to celebrate. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000021||Patrick||12-23-1999||05:36 PM||||<BR>Hey fiero56, who's asking you to sit around? I also think it's kind of neat that the calendar is now going to start with "20" instead of "19", but why do you need to deceive yourself that it's the "new millennium" to celebrate? <P>What irks me the most is the wheeler-dealers who hope to profit from this new millennium hysteria. It's the same people promoting it this year who will also be promoting it NEXT year.<P>By the way, I only gave my two cents worth earlier because Richard brought up the subject... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000022||fiero56||12-23-1999||09:27 PM||||The people trying to sell more due to the millenium "change" irratate me a little. I never thought of what you said though. "I bet they do the same thing next year." Around here we have a TON of diamond dealers talking about "the christmas of the millenium, buy her somethin' nice" stuff. Even Lexus is putting out commercials on TV for their cars and SUVs. I see your point. Well taken, I hope others have seen the light now.||||reg||1
Z||000023||theogre||12-23-1999||10:13 PM||||year one sucked too. It was only slightly better than when all the dinosaurs got whacked by that commet. Man was that a long winter.||||reg||1
