Z||000029||William Federle||12-24-1999||07:33 AM||||I think the big thing about the millenium is<BR>that even tho its not another 1000 years yet<BR>(the date didn't start on the year 0) the<BR>effects of the new millenium will begin<BR>in about 1 week (next Saturday) when the<BR>last two digits of the year turn over to 0.<BR>I personally don't think it will be that big<BR>of a deal - but if I'm wrong it sure won't<BR>be the first time.<P>On the subject of Jesus, I don't like to wear<BR>my religeous beliefs on my sleeve, but I'll just break with that practice long enough to<BR>say that I think that more and more people - <BR>and younger people are believing in him - and<BR>not just in word but in practice. Look at the<BR>young girl at Columbine who gave up her life<BR>rather than say she didn't. It's almost like<BR>the stories of the martyrs in the coleseum in<BR>Rome. Thats all I've got to say about that.<BR>||||reg||1
